WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.148
(playful instrumental music)

00:00:01.148 --> 00:00:04.898
- [Narrator] This is
Zawadi, an African Lion.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:10.306
These stunning big cats
are Africa's apex predator.

00:00:11.417 --> 00:00:13.280
They once roamed most of Africa

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.084
and parts of Europe and Asia,

00:00:16.084 --> 00:00:17.673
but today they are only found

00:00:17.673 --> 00:00:20.340
in parts of Sub-Saharan Africa.

00:00:21.786 --> 00:00:25.953
Zawadi is a male lion,
indicated by his large mane.

00:00:27.205 --> 00:00:28.943
Lions are considered
the only social member

00:00:28.943 --> 00:00:33.110
of the cat family, and live
in large groups called prides.

00:00:34.889 --> 00:00:37.683
Females do most of the
hunting and work in teams,

00:00:37.683 --> 00:00:40.231
ambushing their prey.

00:00:40.231 --> 00:00:42.908
Their importance to the
ecosystem is paramount,

00:00:42.908 --> 00:00:45.216
playing a key role in the food chain,

00:00:45.216 --> 00:00:48.691
controlling herbivore populations,

00:00:48.691 --> 00:00:50.533
but while they are the alpha predators,

00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:52.869
they face threats of their own.

00:00:52.869 --> 00:00:55.706
A combination of trophy
hunting and habitat loss

00:00:55.706 --> 00:00:59.873
has cut their population in
half over the past two decades.

00:01:00.752 --> 00:01:02.835
This is the African lion.

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:11.683
(gentle instrumental music)

